{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create a local certificate authority on node1 named “OS Comparison Root CA.”","status":"satisfied","summary":"A self-signed CA certificate and matching valid private key were created locally. The certificate has the exact CN, CA:TRUE and certificate-signing constraints; the root-owned private key is mode 0600. These properties persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1b02f5fe686640b7","cmd-c4c7caa7f323463c","cmd-06cf22c4ca0847e5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install the CA certificate as a trusted system certificate authority.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The certificate was installed in the native RHEL trust-anchor directory and incorporated into system trust. Both the root and a leaf certificate issued by it verified successfully, p11-kit reported it as an authority anchor, and an unrelated root remained untrusted. Trust persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4e1d767d650e47e4","cmd-282db3059b0d498a","cmd-06cf22c4ca0847e5","cmd-6e8440ce16ad4cc5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were identical before and after execution and restart. The only installed package was the OpenSSL 3.2.2 CLI matching the already-installed OpenSSL libraries; no package upgrades occurred.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ca8035090d6b441e","cmd-1842fa6ca4454c7b","cmd-300bc95217f34c32","cmd-06cf22c4ca0847e5","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the matching OpenSSL CLI was a necessary prerequisite (cmd-300bc95217f34c32); CA creation and trust installation directly implemented the task (cmd-1b02f5fe686640b7, cmd-4e1d767d650e47e4); temporary verification credentials were bounded and removed (cmd-282db3059b0d498a, cmd-06cf22c4ca0847e5, cmd-6e8440ce16ad4cc5); and the reboot served the mandatory restart protocol (cmd-0f29599cda084a40). Final observations showed no failed services, unchanged listener roles, healthy package management, and no task-related temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-300bc95217f34c32","cmd-1b02f5fe686640b7","cmd-4e1d767d650e47e4","cmd-282db3059b0d498a","cmd-0f29599cda084a40","cmd-06cf22c4ca0847e5","cmd-6e8440ce16ad4cc5","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot scheduling, transient loss of connectivity, a changed boot identity, and recovered CA trust, artifacts, services, listeners, and platform state. The lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
